  "summary": "Simplified, functional interiors characterized by clean lines, rounded forms, and modest ornamentation.",
  "description": "Biedermeier interiors feature light-colored woods, curved furniture forms, geometric patterns, and a focus on comfort and functionality. This style emerged in German-speaking regions following the Napoleonic Wars, reflecting a desire for simplicity, domesticity, and bourgeois values in contrast to the preceding Empire style.",
